 "_aesthetic": "Nan, 2026-09-19: 'all pictures should also pass aesthetic tests.' `aes` is Apple Photos' own ZOVERALLAESTHETICSCORE for that frame, carried here so the bar is a number anyone can check rather than a taste. The floor is 0.38 — MY number, not hers, set on the day by looking at where the frames stopped being worth a full screen; tests/test_home.py enforces it and prints the lowest that passed. The Commons picks in image_picks.json are outside it: those Nan chose by hand and her eye is the test there.",
 "floor": 0.38,
 "_background": "bg=true means the frame carries a whole screen behind the words: a scene with depth. bg=false is a close-up — a mask, a plate, a door — which reads well at tile size and turns to abstract colour when it is blown up to fill a phone. Tiles draw from both; the scenes only from bg."
}